{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1538274-true-faith-spend-and-regain-20th","id":1538274,"title":"True Faith : spend and regain 20th","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-08T19:11:19-07:00","id":1538274,"title":"True Faith : spend and regain 20th","content":"So i am trying to find any infos on how to regain dots of true faith when we use it. Nor if you lose a dot when you do. So, as i understand, you can remake a roll every round. Seems abusive, especially if it says you can spend a TF instead of a Will. <br /> <br /> I told my player that he spend a TF dot to create a miracle, then have to prey at least one hour to regain the dot. Still, feel the need to see if there is a real mechanics for it and i can't find infos anywhere. Si i am asking for help here. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28291-castlenight","name":"CastleNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T08:46:51-07:00","id":1538301,"title":"","content":"I think an important question would be &quot;which version of 20th&quot;?<br /> <br /> Pretty sure the rules for how it works are different depending on which gameline you are playing. But I've never encountered any version that works in the fashion you've described either, being used for re-rolls or spending &quot;temporary points/dots&quot; in order to achieve its effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T14:06:49-07:00","id":1538322,"title":"","content":"It's simpler to just limit its use to once a scene or once a chapter.<br /> <br /> True Faith is heavily based on ST fiat, so the best answer is for it to work when and how you want, give or take some actions like rebuking vampires, where it does make sense for the player to have some expectations that it'll work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-10T10:53:15-07:00","id":1538373,"title":"","content":"I don't recall ever seeing True Faith treated as a spendable resource. Just as a rating that can add to dice pools or be rolled itself for certain effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T11:14:00-07:00","id":1539046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1538274-true-faith-spend-and-regain-20th?p=1538301#post1538301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think an important question would be &quot;which version of 20th&quot;?<br /> <br /> Pretty sure the rules for how it works are different depending on which gameline you are playing. But I've never encountered any version that works in the fashion you've described either, being used for re-rolls or spending &quot;temporary points/dots&quot; in order to achieve its effects.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1538274-true-faith-spend-and-regain-20th?p=1538373#post1538373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall ever seeing True Faith treated as a spendable resource. Just as a rating that can add to dice pools or be rolled itself for certain effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Older versions of true faith acted like a second willpower rating that stacked with willpower and had its own points. It functions that way in &quot;Kinfolk: a breed apart&quot; as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T17:00:53-07:00","id":1539066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1538274-true-faith-spend-and-regain-20th?p=1539046#post1539046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Older versions of true faith acted like a second willpower rating that stacked with willpower and had its own points. It functions that way in &quot;Kinfolk: a breed apart&quot; as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would explain why I haven't seen it before, my experience with pre-20 books is rather spotty.<br /> <br /> If it's only in earlier editions, you'd need to find the appropriate texts (like the above-mentioned Kinfolk book) to refer to. I'm fairly sure the core rules for V20 and M20 don't work like that, but less sure about the other anniversary editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T18:38:37-07:00","id":1539125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1538274-true-faith-spend-and-regain-20th?p=1538373#post1538373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall ever seeing True Faith treated as a spendable resource. Just as a rating that can add to dice pools or be rolled itself for certain effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Mage 20th, in a block, as alternate rules for true faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28291-castlenight","name":"CastleNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T20:21:55-07:00","id":1539363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1538274-true-faith-spend-and-regain-20th?p=1539066#post1539066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would explain why I haven't seen it before, my experience with pre-20 books is rather spotty.<br /> <br /> If it's only in earlier editions, you'd need to find the appropriate texts (like the above-mentioned Kinfolk book) to refer to. I'm fairly sure the core rules for V20 and M20 don't work like that, but less sure about the other anniversary editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The kinfolk book is part of WTA20, and as<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28291-castlenight\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28291\" data-vbnamecard=\"28291\">CastleNight</a> mensioned, the M20 rules have it working as the VTM20 or WTA20 system depending on which rules you use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-27T08:50:09-07:00","id":1539377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1538274-true-faith-spend-and-regain-20th?p=1539363#post1539363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The kinfolk book is part of WTA20, and as<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28291-castlenight\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28291\" data-vbnamecard=\"28291\">CastleNight</a> mensioned, the M20 rules have it working as the VTM20 or WTA20 system depending on which rules you use.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, my mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T10:08:56-07:00","id":1541236,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your answers. Helped me greatly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> So, my player can use true faith the way we fit the must usefull and fun to use. Her faith is centered around her knowledge of the Book of Nod and Cain. She's a Tremere with humanity 10 and it's pretty challenging for her. (Yeah we tweaked that together) She can use her faith once a day, and to regain it she must pray. She's not an abusive player so it works perfectly. She knows there is a big chance she lose her True Faith cause the game setting is starting to be a little bit too hardcore. (All Tremere players) Her Regent doesnt have her true faith and humanity in priority. Tho, he may tries to protect her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28291-castlenight","name":"CastleNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}